kind: InlineAgentSkill
content: |
  ---
  name: exception-email-drafting
  description: Drafts a professional HTML email to the vendor or internal team about an Accounts Payable invoice exception or error, shows the draft for review, and sends it only after explicit user approval. Use it only after the user agrees to draft an email for a three-way match exception.
  ---
  <!-- bic:source=blank -->
   Exception Email Drafting

  Trigger: ONLY after the user answers "yes" to "Would you like me to draft an email for
  this exception?"

  Steps:
  1. Find the exception and the recommended action from the validation result.
  2. Find the recipient:
     - Vendor-facing issues (quantity, price, total, duplicate invoice): use the vendor
       email from the New Purchase Order record.
     - Internal issues (GR reversal, over receipt, partial receipt, vendor mismatch,
       PO/GR not found): ask the user who should receive it.
     - If no email address is available, ask the user for it. Never guess an address.
  3. Draft the email:
     Subject: Invoice <Invoice No.> – <Exception> – PO <PO No.>
     Body (HTML): greeting; a one-line statement of the issue; a small table with
     Invoice No., PO No., GR No., Item, Qty Ordered/Received/Invoiced, Unit Price
     (PO/Invoice) and Invoice Total; the requested action and a response date; a polite
     closing signed by the Accounts Payable team. Do not include bank or payment details.
  4. Show the full draft (To, Subject, Body) to the user, then ask exactly:
     "Do you approve this email for sending?"
  5. If the user requests changes: revise the draft, show it again, and ask again.
     If the user declines: do not send. Confirm that nothing was sent.
  6. Send ONLY after an explicit "yes" or "approve", using the Send email (Office 365
     Outlook) tool with these parameters:
       to: <recipient email>
       subject: <email subject line>
       body: <formatted HTML string>
       isHtmlBody: true
  7. Confirm that the email was sent (recipient, subject, time) and add it to the audit note.

  Never send automatically, never send to an address the user has not seen, and never
  send more than one email per approval.
